* dial-me-spinner/detent-stepper view "step_emf" (breadboard.dev, Apache-2.0): the detent stepper's
* two phases on J40 with the back-EMF of a rotor turning at pps full steps per second from t0 to
* tstop (E3's step case: examples/dial-me-spinner/e3/board-step.cir's BEMFA and BEMFB, the suite's
* KE_MAX 1.37 V per k step/s and load angle pi/2; motor_drive__stepper.lib's PMSTEP_PHASE, phase A
* -E sin, phase B +E cos). The EMF is a V-type B source in series with the phase's 20 Ohm and
* 4.3 mH, as in board-step.cir (no milliohm path, so phase0 holds; AGENTS.md).
* Ports: Pin_1 Pin_2 (phase A), Pin_3 Pin_4 (phase B).
.subckt dms_detent_stepper_step_emf PA1 PA2 PB1 PB2 params: r=20 l=4.3m ke=1.37 pps=446
+ delta=1.5707963267949 t0=0 tstop=0
.param emf_e = {ke*pps/1000}
.param emf_w = {2*3.14159265358979*pps/4}
RA PA1 a_l {r}
LA a_l a_e {l}
BEMFA a_e PA2 V = (time > t0 && time < tstop) ? emf_e*(-sin(emf_w*(time - t0) - delta)) : 0
RB PB1 b_l {r}
LB b_l b_e {l}
BEMFB b_e PB2 V = (time > t0 && time < tstop) ? emf_e*cos(emf_w*(time - t0) - delta) : 0
.ends dms_detent_stepper_step_emf
